    <item>
      <title>Behavioural and Online Testing</title>
      <link>https://lisn-lab.org/facilities/behaviour/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 07 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://lisn-lab.org/facilities/behaviour/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We run behavioural studies in quiet, dedicated testing booths at Lancaster University to measure how inner speech shapes perception, attention, and decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside campus testing, our institutional Pavlovia platform lets us run online experiments with wider, more diverse participant groups.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Eye Tracking</title>
      <link>https://lisn-lab.org/facilities/eyetracking/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 07 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://lisn-lab.org/facilities/eyetracking/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Our EyeLink 1000 eye-tracking system records tiny eye movements, gaze shifts, and pupil changes in real time. Because gaze and pupil size reflect attention, arousal, and uncertainty, eye tracking lets us observe how inner speech coordinates with visual perception during reading and problem solving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also use portable Tobii eye trackers for studies outside the lab.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>High-density EEG with 3D digitisation</title>
      <link>https://lisn-lab.org/facilities/eeg/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 07 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://lisn-lab.org/facilities/eeg/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We use a 128-channel EGI electroencephalography (EEG) system to record electrical brain activity millisecond by millisecond as people read, think silently, or solve problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Polhemus Fastrak 3D scanner maps the exact position of each sensor on a participant&amp;rsquo;s head, improving our ability to trace where those signals arise in the brain.&lt;/p&gt;

















